\name{gf_tcga_pan_cancer_survival}
\alias{gf_tcga_pan_cancer_survival}
\encoding{UTF-8}
\title{Is one gene's expression associated with overall survival in each TCGA cancer?}
\description{Is one gene's expression associated with overall survival in each TCGA cancer? GeneFox's Pan-Cancer Survival screen: per cohort, a median split of baseline-tumor patients, Kaplan-Meier log-rank p, Cox HR, and BH q-values across the 33 PanCanAtlas cohorts, with the forest plot (or one cohort's Kaplan-Meier with cohort=). Survival is PanCanAtlas OS, not the GDC clinical OS tcga_survival uses. Latency: 1-4 min cold (33 cohorts x 4 requests), seconds when cached. The forest and cohort Kaplan-Meier figures are the app's PNG exports.}
\usage{
gf_tcga_pan_cancer_survival(
    session,
    `gene`,
    `cohort` = NULL,
    `csv` = NULL,
    `dpi` = NULL,
    `figure` = NULL,
    `format` = NULL,
    `height_in` = NULL,
    `html` = NULL,
    `inline_image` = NULL,
    `output_name` = NULL,
    `recipe` = NULL,
    `scrub_at_years` = NULL,
    `show_caption_color_keys` = NULL,
    `show_figure_legends` = NULL,
    `show_row_counts` = NULL,
    `size` = NULL,
    `survival_detail` = NULL,
    `width_in` = NULL,
    progress_callback = NULL
)
}
\arguments{
\item{session}{A GeneFox session from \code{\link{gf_session}}.}
\item{gene}{(string) HGNC gene symbol, e.g. CLDN18. Upper-cased, as the app does.}
\item{cohort}{(string, optional; one of "TCGA-ACC", "TCGA-BLCA", "TCGA-BRCA", "TCGA-CESC", "TCGA-CHOL", "TCGA-COAD", "TCGA-DLBC", "TCGA-ESCA", "TCGA-GBM", "TCGA-HNSC", "TCGA-KICH", "TCGA-KIRC", "TCGA-KIRP", "TCGA-LAML", "TCGA-LGG", "TCGA-LIHC", "TCGA-LUAD", "TCGA-LUSC", "TCGA-MESO", "TCGA-OV", "TCGA-PAAD", "TCGA-PCPG", "TCGA-PRAD", "TCGA-READ", "TCGA-SARC", "TCGA-SKCM", "TCGA-STAD", "TCGA-TGCT", "TCGA-THCA", "TCGA-THYM", "TCGA-UCEC", "TCGA-UCS", "TCGA-UVM") Draw this cohort's Kaplan-Meier from the same sweep instead of the forest plot. NULL omits it.}
\item{csv}{(boolean, optional; default false) Also write the screen's CSV export (the app's own rows) under the output directory and return csv.path. NULL omits it.}
\item{dpi}{(integer, optional; default 300; range 72..1200) Resolution of a custom size (at most 8,192 px a side and 16 MP). NULL omits it.}
\item{figure}{(boolean, optional; default true) Draw the figure and return its PNG path. NULL omits it.}
\item{format}{(string, optional; one of "png", "svg", "tiff"; default "png") File format the figure is written as: png (raster, the default), svg (vector, with its labels as editable text), or tiff (raster, .tif, for journal submission). Every figure is written in all three formats. NULL omits it.}
\item{height_in}{(number, optional; range 1..40) Custom figure height in inches (with the other side; instead of size). The app's size control range. NULL omits it.}
\item{html}{(boolean, optional; default false) Also write the screen's single-figure HTML export (the app's own document: title, subtitle, source, the figure and its table, plus the figure's alt text as the image alt and its data table) under the output directory and return html.path. Needs figure. NULL omits it.}
